sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-14> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Cells may physiologically disconnect from the tissue network (e.g. closing gap junctions under prolonged stress), and each reduction in connectivity makes local computation easier and further gap-junction closure more likely, a positive feedback loop of dissociation that makes tissue-level goals ever harder to achieve; Levin presents this as consistent with gap-junction closure in early transformation and with tumours induced by non-carcinogenic geometric barriers.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Gap-junction closure in transformation is a positive feedback loop of isolation";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Multiscale Wisdom of the Body: Collective Intelligence as a Tractable Interface for Next-Generation Biomedicine”, BioEssays : news and reviews in molecular, cellular and developmental biology (2025), doi:10.1002/bies.202400196; section “Cancer and the Scaling of the Self”. Scope: Early carcinogenic transformation in animal tissues"
}
